# One construction lifecycle on an ordinary founded settlement: the production founding
# transaction, a startup census of what the settlement actually holds, the production
# quote/CanPay/commission with its physical timber and water debit, real engine turns spent by
# the bounded advance verb, and the completion of that exact job into a functional building,
# followed by a real save a separate cold-load profile can be imported from.
#
# Nothing is fabricated: no stock is minted and no job is forced into a phase. The settlement
# pays out of its own accumulated stores, so lifecycle-build refuses honestly when the economy
# has not yet paid for the design, and lifecycle-grown refuses when the turn budget expires
# before the building stands. Both refusals are the point of the persona, not a failure of it.
#
# The cold-load session and the next action after it are NOT in this script: they need a second
# profile imported from this save. Tools/check-quickstart-lifecycle.py reports them as BLOCKER
# until that leg exists, and never as a pass.
DESCRIPTION=one paid commission becomes a finished building over real turns, then a real save
REQUEST=founding-first-city
START=8.22@40,12
SCRIPT=stagedigest;realize;lifecycle-open;advance 600;lifecycle-build;advance 2400;lifecycle-grown;lifecycle-save;stagedigest
VERBS=lifecycle-open,lifecycle-build,lifecycle-grown,lifecycle-save
EXPECT=stagedigest:OK~founded=false,realize:OK,lifecycle-open:OK~step=startup,advance:OK,lifecycle-build:OK~step=paid-commission,advance:OK,lifecycle-grown:OK~step=engine-turn-build,lifecycle-save:OK~step=save,stagedigest:OK~founded=true,COMPLETE
SET=growth,construction,native-regression
TIMEOUT=1200
